// Application icon for the Coordinator binaries (NutriculaLicenseService.exe
// and NutriculaLicenseBroker.exe). Windows Explorer and Task Manager's
// "Details" tab both show the icon with the LOWEST resource ID in an exe's
// resources as its "main" icon - hence ID 1 here, matching the convention
// the C# Installer itself already follows for its own icon.
//
// Shared by both build_Broker_*.bat and build_Service_*.bat (see their own
// comments) - both binaries get the same Nutricula icon, since to a user in
// Task Manager they are both just "Nutricula" processes.
//
// The referenced icon.ico is resolved relative to THIS .rc file's own
// location (standard windres/cpp #include-style resolution, independent of
// whatever directory a build script happens to be invoked from) - so this
// path must stay in sync with icon.ico's actual location at the repository
// root, two levels up from this Coordinator folder.
1 ICON "../../icon.ico"
